From f6a4baacf2addd6d4c4fdebc0be37ac1ec6549b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 117/118] wifi: ath10k: restart the firmware when a key install
 times out

ath10k_install_key() sends WMI_VDEV_INSTALL_KEY_CMDID and waits 3 s for
the firmware to acknowledge it. If the firmware does not answer, the
function returns -ETIMEDOUT, every caller logs it, and that is the end of
it: the driver carries on talking to a firmware that has demonstrably
stopped servicing its control path, with the key state in the firmware
now unknown.

On a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, WCN3990 hw1.0) this is not a recoverable
situation. Observed on an idle station link:

  ath10k_snoc 18800000.wifi: failed to install key for vdev 0 peer ...: -110
  wlan0: failed to remove key (0, ...) from hardware (-110)
  wpa_supplicant: wlan0: CTRL-EVENT-DISCONNECTED ... reason=4 locally_generated=1

From that point the firmware kept doing 802.11 management on its own -
eight further associations all completed with status=0 - but returned a
drop completion for every data frame, so no EAPOL frame ever left the
chip and none of those associations reached the 4-way handshake. The
firmware never crashed, so no existing ath10k recovery trigger fired and
the interface stayed unusable until the machine was rebooted. Recovering
at the point of the key timeout would have cost one firmware restart
instead of an indefinitely dead interface.

Treat the unanswered install-key command the same way ath10k_wmi_cmd_send()
already treats a WMI command it cannot hand to the firmware within 3 s, and
ask for a firmware restart. ath10k_core_start_recovery() is a no-op unless
the device is running and no recovery is already pending, and it does not
block on the restart, so this stays a single queued restart even if several
key installs time out in a row.

The hook goes in ath10k_install_key() rather than in its callers so that
every path that installs a key - .set_key, the static WEP key upload, and
the peer key teardown - is covered.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 4db75dc91eb7..8431f33e9653 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -326,8 +326,12 @@ static int ath10k_install_key(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
 		return ret;
 
 	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ar->install_key_done, 3 * HZ);
-	if (time_left == 0)
+	if (time_left == 0) {
+		ath10k_warn(ar, "vdev %i install key timed out, restarting hardware\n",
+			    arvif->vdev_id);
+		ath10k_core_start_recovery(ar);
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
